      "writtenOn": "2023-10-06T19:50:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let me explain why having a connection is required. In the AIDL model, device ports of external devices are \"templates\" (regardless whether the device has dynamic profiles or not). Once the device is connected, a real device port is created, with address assigned (if any). For permanently attached devices, the device port is the real device port, and its address is fixed. If we set up remote submix input as a permanently attached device, it could only have one device port, with one address. Obviously, this will not work for the screen capture scenario.\n\nAnd we can\u0027t have a permanently attached and a removable device port of the same device type because device attachment ability is associated with the device type.\n\n\u003e Not supporting this means that we get rid of supporting \"legacy\" remote submix devices (Address \"0\") in audio policy?\n\nI will find or write a test for this scenario. Since it\u0027s legacy, I\u0027m not sure how important is it. If needed, I will implement connection of remote submix device with address 0 in libaudiohal@aidl.",
      "parentUuid": "38c5539b_668e391f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 112,
        "startChar": 40,
        "endLine": 113,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "30b0b40b83af989f8c9801b650e1354ccd712fb7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
