        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 123,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-06T19:50:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can update that, however the major obstacle is that currently there is only one version of the remote submix configuration—since it did not have any lists with more than one element, it remained compatible both with pre-7.0 and 7.0 parsers. If we want to bring the XML file on par with this configuration for AIDL, we will also have to add lists for sample rates and channel masks. This will require forking the config file for pre-7.0 and 7.0, and updating bunch of other resources: other .xml files that include it, and Android.bp files. Not sure all of this worth the effort.\n\nSince it has turned out that the canonical configuration has that many exceptions compared to what we expect for the AIDL implementation, and it was unlikely that partners actually modified it, to me it seems easier to provide a hardcoded configuration instead. This also aligns with the fact that in the long term we plan to move remote submix module to the framework side because it does not depend on the silicon or on anything in the kernel.",
      "parentUuid": "ec499817_05720879",
